<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12097"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 1:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is for any kind of comments anyone might have on the above, &#34;FROM LAW ENFORCEMENT to this Board&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12097-->
<!--Post: 12122--><!--Time: 1111610726-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12122"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 12:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lawyers might also be able to answer some of these types of questions<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12122-->
<!--Post: 12144--><!--Time: 1111644961-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12144"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why would any LE or Lawyer directly involved inside the case be willing to release information to a group of citizens ? Why would they be compelled to even revisit this site once they captured Rader? <BR> <BR>Finally why after 35 yrs of not sharing info would LE decide now is the time ?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12144-->
<!--Post: 12147--><!--Time: 1111647280-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12147"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 23, 2005 - 10:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wouldn&#39;t expect anyone involved directly in this case responding either, however we did on this site for example have a Florida cop who worked on a unsolved multiple murder case post here and tell us how that got solved. We&#39;ve had a lawyer or two post here also. It would be interesting to get the thoughts and analysis from anyone with professional law enforcement and judicial credentials to give their insight to us citizens.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12147-->
<!--Post: 12157--><!--Time: 1111678641-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12157"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 7:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Go Johno!  I think it is a GREAT idea!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12157-->
<!--Post: 12181--><!--Time: 1111717247-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12181"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 6:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, <BR> <BR>and to a lesser extent Elsewhere. Guess what most people forget when they are on the internet ? Identity and reality are very difficult to verify. Any kid can log on and pretend to be a woman.  .  .   <BR> <BR>In our case someone who claims to be a cop most likely is a &#34;wanna-be&#34; cop who derives pleasure in pretending he is something he is not.  <BR> <BR>Since we have no form of verification of a person&#39;s true identity it is unlikely that we could expect actual case detectives to respond or police officers to respond to this site.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Unless the FLA cop is giving his true name and badge # we don&#39;t really know that person&#39;s true identity.  .  . <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12181-->
<!--Post: 12182--><!--Time: 1111718791-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12182"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 6:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Now you sound like a cop. <BR>Give us your thoughts over on the &#39;From Law Enforcement&#39; thread. So far nobody&#39;s even pretending to be a cop over there so if you are not then pretend that you are and we&#39;ll discuss it over here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12182-->
<!--Post: 12189--><!--Time: 1111724564-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12189"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 8:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, <BR> <BR>Common sense is what I am talking about. It doesn&#39;t take a cop or a lawyer or a brain surgeon to figure out that many people &#34;spoof&#34; good people like you and me and the majority of posters on this board. <BR> <BR>I am not trying to be a jerk; I am very wary as I have had people attempt to scam me. That includes the girl who says shes is something and then turns out to WAY more something than I bargained for to the stupid letters from &#34;officials&#34; in  Nigeria asking me if I would like to accept a 20% commission on $10 mil dollars if I will just agree to let them deposit the funds in my  American checking account.  .  .    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12189-->
<!--Post: 12190--><!--Time: 1111728543-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12190"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 24, 2005 - 9:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You are correct, Tac - there is a significant chance that a thread for LE will draw a faker, or two, or three.  But after dealing with a bunch of fake BTKs, and possibly drawing the real thing a time or two, I&#39;m willing to risk sorting the wheat from the chaff, LE-wise.  As you suggest with the Nigerian scam letters we all get, there&#39;s a lot of crap out there.  But it&#39;s just par for the internet course.  My kids and I laugh at their fellow teen posters sometimes, sharing our thoughts on which ones are Michael Jackson, or which might be FBI guardian angels trolling for Disney execs trolling for kids. <BR> <BR>Frankly, I don&#39;t expect answers from Detective W.P.D. Btkbuster.  I&#39;m hoping to hear from some retired bald Indiana cop who lurks the thread and remembers something from a similar case and has an opinion.  And if some junior high kid can come off like one, I want to hear it just for the yuks.  It&#39;s always interesting to see how far the fakers get before I&#39;m wise.  Bring &#39;em on!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12190-->
<!--Post: 12197--><!--Time: 1111740033-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12197"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 12:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax56 &amp; Johno: Right on! Let&#39;s give the &#34;FROM LAW ENFORCEMENT to this board&#34;- thread a chance. As the saying goes, &#34;You&#39;ll never know unless you ask.&#34;. I wouldn&#39;t expect the Wichita D.A. to post, but other L.E. types may very well. And there&#39;s a good chance that some may even give their real names &amp; ranks, so we can easily verify. <BR> <BR>TAC: Don&#39;t be so darn negative. Just let law enforcement-types post as they see fit. This could be a golden opportunity to get some juicy answers &#34;straight from the horses&#39; mouth.&#34;. I&#39;m sure us &#39;regulars&#39; will find plenty of time to fact-check &amp; verify in our many wondrous ways. &#40;Are you listening, Skov?&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12197-->
<!--Post: 12204--><!--Time: 1111764284-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12204"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 7:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey - on one hand I want to see the posts also...we are all smart enought to figure out the &#34;phonies&#34; and wannabees...but then again part of me agrees with Tac and I understand the wariness...remember Denny Boy...he fooled everyone for YEARS.... <BR>BUT I would so enjoy the posts and the insights.... <BR>Guess I am on both sides of the fence here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12204-->
<!--Post: 12230--><!--Time: 1111789401-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12230"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 2:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->exactly, you guys are very intelligent and by this time we can tell who is who on the board, everyone here knows more informtion than the occasional poster, we know what Rader eats for breakfast for goodness sakes, we also have people in LE that are working hard on this case, I am sure they would tell is if someone was a fake. I the crime Library new chapters on Rader, the auther mentions that becasue of the net boards, they may be able to link Rader to three other murders so no matter wht anyone says, You all are helping. Thanks E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12230-->
<!--Post: 12231--><!--Time: 1111789648-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12231"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 2:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Pax,V,E, <BR> <BR>Ok you have all convinced me to change my stance. Bring it on ! Lets all keep a firm grip on reality; remember many spoofers are very talented. The Nigerian stuff is a complete joke but there are some talented scam artists out there. <BR> <BR>I am on board your case makes much more sense and since we have nothing to lose, keep your wallets in your pockets, then full steam ahead.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12231-->
<!--Post: 12254--><!--Time: 1111807774-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12254"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Pax56<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Pax56<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 25, 2005 - 7:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bravo, Tac - that&#39;s the spirit! <BR> <BR>Now, after we&#39;ve scared off most of the fakers, is ANYBODY going to post?  I&#39;d give it a while - it took some time after Tom put up the &#34;From BTK&#34; thread before we got any BTKs.  And even longer before we got one who was over 21!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12254-->
<!--Post: 12315--><!--Time: 1111972076-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12315"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 5:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not a real cop, but I&#39;ve played one on the radio once...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12315-->
<!--Post: 12322--><!--Time: 1111988208-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12322"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 27, 2005 - 9:36 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m thinking they would be putting their career aspirations in jeapardy by posting, on the internet, concerning a case that has yet to go to trial. We may have to wait until the fat lady sings.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12322-->
<!--Post: 12331--><!--Time: 1111997841-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12331"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 28, 2005 - 12:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B you are right. I believe that may be the answer for our hero Tom V.  <BR> <BR>Btw does it not seem odd that Rader&#39;s bros or family would NOT have known that Dennis was up to horrible things long ago ? <BR> <BR>Pax, <BR> <BR>Thanks for the Bravo !<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12331-->
<!--Post: 12335--><!--Time: 1111999501-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12335"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 28, 2005 - 12:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The first time I heard a cop on TV say he may be walking here among us...he might be your next door neighbor...&#40;or somethink of dat nature&#41; back in the seventies, the first thing I did was go down the list of all male humans in that vague age group and and suspect everyone until I had a list of possibilities whether they were related to me or just worked at the filling station. <BR> <BR>I think what really through everyone off was the fact that he was first described as Hispanic or dark skinned, and by the time anyone said different, most people had gone through the elimination process and grown used to the idea of of BTK just &#34;being part of the scenery&#34;.  <BR> <BR>It was sort of like a rattlesnake in a pasture. You know they are around, and you see them occasionally, But people rarely get bit, and when it happens it seems few and far between. <BR> <BR>So after the possibility was brought up that he might not be Hispanic, Mideastern or even have a tan, no one really went through the reaccessment proccess. <BR> <BR>But...hell yes, with that many close family members close by, and other people who had known him all his life...someone knew, and it will take a lot to convince me otherwise.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12335-->
<!--Post: 12343--><!--Time: 1112023928-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12343"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsewhere<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsewhere<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 28, 2005 - 7:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agreee B - I still think SOMEONE had to have thought something was amiss...I still have wonderment in regards to his wife...this will all be quite interesting.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
